# Introductory learning slides.
onboarding-learn-slide-welcome-title = Welcome, traveler.
onboarding-learn-slide-welcome-body = Before you step into new worlds, here is how everything fits together. Minecraft modding is simpler than it looks — you just need to know the pieces.
onboarding-learn-slide-java-title = Minecraft runs on Java
onboarding-learn-slide-java-body = The programming language called Java was used to build Minecraft. But different versions of Minecraft require different versions of Java. Don't worry, Vesta will handle all the Java stuff for you.
onboarding-learn-slide-mods-title = Mods need a bridge.
onboarding-learn-slide-mods-body = Minecraft was not built for changes. A Modloader is the bridge that allows mods to chane the way you play.
onboarding-learn-slide-loaders-title = Choose your path.
onboarding-learn-slide-loaders-body = Forge and its modern successor, NeoForge, focus on deep, complex game overhauls, while Fabric and its fork, Quilt, prioritize a lightweight, high-performance experience with faster updates. Together, these four loaders represent the choice between heavy-duty content ecosystems and agile, modular performance.
onboarding-learn-slide-modpacks-title = Modpacks are a quick way to get started.
onboarding-learn-slide-modpacks-body = A modpack is a curated collection of mods, configurations, and sometimes custom assets that work together to create a specific gameplay experience. They are an easy way to dive into modded Minecraft without having to pick and choose individual mods yourself.
